WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.498 --> 00:00:01.818
A kettle stops working.

2
00:00:02.756 --> 00:00:04.112
A laptop sits forgotten.

3
00:00:05.027 --> 00:00:06.227
Then a child asks:

4
00:00:06.482 --> 00:00:08.114
does this have to become rubbish?

5
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.672
For one family, a better story begins.

6
00:00:13.738 --> 00:00:14.818
Meet FixForward.

7
00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:18.205
One place to understand everyday electronics

8
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.825
and make thoughtful choices about e-waste.

9
00:00:21.693 --> 00:00:23.049
Start by learning together,

10
00:00:23.207 --> 00:00:24.623
or get help with an item.

11
00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:28.491
Turn a digital appliance around.

12
00:00:29.393 --> 00:00:30.845
Discover what its parts do,

13
00:00:31.051 --> 00:00:32.768
and explore simple care habits.

14
00:00:33.768 --> 00:00:35.260
Big ideas become something

15
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.289
your family can see.

16
00:00:38.346 --> 00:00:39.654
Now, try a choice.

17
00:00:40.604 --> 00:00:43.318
This working laptop has been checked by an adult.

18
00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:46.479
Repair, reuse, or recycle?

19
00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.087
Reuse could give it another chapter.

20
00:00:50.003 --> 00:00:51.575
Every answer explains why.

21
00:00:53.674 --> 00:00:56.292
For a real item, an adult takes the lead.

22
00:00:57.146 --> 00:00:58.117
Choose its category,

23
00:00:58.288 --> 00:01:01.074
or try the optional photo helper where available.

24
00:01:01.917 --> 00:01:02.961
It suggests a type,

25
00:01:03.071 --> 00:01:04.307
not a diagnosis.

26
00:01:06.674 --> 00:01:09.448
Consider warning signs and check recall information

27
00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.155
before choosing your next step.

28
00:01:12.057 --> 00:01:14.194
Children can spot questions to ask.

29
00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.838
Adults handle real appliances

30
00:01:16.877 --> 00:01:18.569
and arrange qualified help.

31
00:01:20.562 --> 00:01:22.267
Explore repair when suitable,

32
00:01:22.377 --> 00:01:24.550
reuse when an item is safe and wanted,

33
00:01:24.649 --> 00:01:26.293
or appropriate recycling.

34
00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:28.851
Check the service and what it accepts

35
00:01:28.865 --> 00:01:29.693
before visiting.

36
00:01:32.562 --> 00:01:34.808
Back at home, the conversation changes.

37
00:01:35.781 --> 00:01:37.798
Let's find out before we throw it away.

38
00:01:38.762 --> 00:01:40.996
A small discovery becomes a useful habit,

39
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:42.486
shared across the family.

40
00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:45.365
FixForward.

41
00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:49.077
Little discoveries. Better choices.

42
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:52.322
Learn together, or get help with an item.

43
00:01:53.226 --> 00:01:54.931
A better next step starts here.
